# TODO: bring benchmarks in line with the research spec

Status: done.

## Core execution model

- Removed StarPU-only comparison modes from the main benchmark matrix:
  - removed `starpu_cpu`;
  - removed `starpu_gpu`;
  - kept only `native_cpu`, `native_gpu`, `starpu_hybrid`.
- StarPU is evaluated as a heterogeneous scheduler, not as a wrapper around CPU-only/GPU-only execution.
- Updated `ExecutionMode`, CLI help, README, scripts, and experiment matrix.

## Native baselines

- Added `native_cpu` and `native_gpu` implementations for every main scenario:
  - `matmul`;
  - `independent`;
  - `heterogeneous`;
  - `image`.
- Replaced BLAS/cuBLAS baselines with simple scalar CPU loops and straightforward CUDA kernels.
- Kept native baselines intentionally simple so the comparison focuses on scheduling rather than tuned library performance.

## Matrix multiplication

- Replaced the monolithic StarPU matmul task with a tiled implementation.
- StarPU now submits independent output-tile tasks.
- Default matrix sizes in `scripts/run_all_experiments.sh`:
  - 512x512;
  - 1024x1024;
  - 2048x2048.
- JSON metrics record tile size and submitted task count.

## Independent tasks

- Replaced the matvec workload with independent array processing:
  `y[i] = sin(x[i]) + sqrt(x[i]) + x[i]^2`.
- Each StarPU task processes a separate block.
- Added all three main modes:
  - native CPU;
  - native GPU;
  - StarPU hybrid.
- The experiment matrix varies task count.
- JSON metrics record task count, block size, total elements, and average task time.

## Heterogeneous workload

- Redesigned the scenario around three task classes:
  - light array tasks;
  - medium array tasks;
  - heavy array tasks.
- Added native CPU and native GPU baselines.
- Kept StarPU hybrid as the only StarPU mode.
- StarPU submits mixed task classes together to create uneven load.
- JSON metrics record counts per task class, sizes per class, total elements, and aggregate runtime.

## Image / edge-oriented scenario

- Kept image tiling for StarPU.
- Added operations:
  - grayscale;
  - blur;
  - edge detection;
  - convolution;
  - filtering.
- Fixed GPU blur so it performs a real 3x3 blur instead of falling back to grayscale.
- Fixed native CPU image path so it uses a normal CPU function.
- Documented simplified per-tile no-halo border handling in JSON metadata.
- Added native CPU and native GPU paths for all selected operations.
- JSON metrics record image size, tile size, operation, tile count, and border policy.

## Metrics and output files

- Every benchmark writes a machine-readable JSON result file.
- JSON result files include:
  - scenario;
  - mode;
  - input parameters;
  - total runtime;
  - task count where applicable;
  - block/tile size where applicable;
  - StarPU overhead breakdown fields where applicable;
  - path to system metrics CSV;
  - StarPU trace prefix.
- `run_experiment.sh` exports the system metrics CSV path so benchmarks link it in result metadata.

## StarPU overhead

- Kept `bench_overhead` as an auxiliary noop/memcpy microbenchmark.
- Added per-scenario StarPU timing fields where applicable:
  - StarPU initialization time;
  - data registration time;
  - task submission time;
  - wait/synchronization time;
  - data unregister/copy-back time.
- Real workload comparisons should use native total time vs StarPU hybrid total time plus the per-scenario StarPU breakdown.

## Remove unused benchmark

- Removed `hello_starpu`.
- Deleted it from:
  - CMake target list;
  - README;
  - run scripts;
  - experiment matrix;
  - source tree.

## Documentation

- Rewrote README around the final three modes:
  - `native_cpu`;
  - `native_gpu`;
  - `starpu_hybrid`.
- Updated integration notes to distinguish:
  - implementation complexity;
  - scheduling overhead;
  - data movement overhead;
  - limitations of each scenario.
- Documented hardware/platform deviation separately from benchmark methodology.
